The PowerGlove Serial Interface (PGSI) is a small device measuring 3.35" by
1" by 1.5" that connects to any DB-25 style RS-232 connector.  The device
should work with any IBM, IBM-compatible, Amiga, Macintosh, Workstation, or
other type of computer that has a serial port.  The device interfaces the
PowerGlove and/or SEGA-style shutter glasses to the computer, and
communicates with them using standard RS-232 data values.  The interface
emulates both of the AGE Menelli command sets, has extensions to allow the
user to read and write values from and to a digital port, and can be
reprogrammed with code updates by the end-user.

NOTE: The software that comes with the PGSI is all public domain software.
In most cases, it is supported or maintained by anyone at ACM @ UIUC.

